# Handoff prompt ordering

- A next-session or end-of-session handoff prompt is the final operation of an implementation session.
- Do not generate the handoff after local implementation or local verification alone.
- Generate it only after the completed work has been committed, pushed, and the pushed remote CI/result has been checked and confirmed working.
- If commit/push has not been explicitly authorized yet, stop before the handoff prompt and report that the implementation is awaiting commit/push authorization.
- After authorization, commit and push, confirm the remote result once, then print the fresh-session prompt last.
